      <!-- Detailed Review: BirkyStudio -->
      <h2 style="font-size:1.6rem;font-weight:700;color:white;margin-bottom:32px;">Detailed Reviews</h2>

      <div id="birky-studio" style="background:rgba(255,45,149,0.08);border:1px solid rgba(255,45,149,0.3);border-radius:16px;padding:32px;margin-bottom:32px;">
        <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;margin-bottom:16px;">
          <span style="background:var(--bs-accent);color:white;padding:4px 12px;border-radius:100px;font-size:0.75rem;font-weight:600;">IT ANSWERS FOR YOU</span>
          <h3 style="color:white;font-size:1.3rem;margin:0;">BirkyStudio</h3>
        </div>
        <p style="color:var(--bs-text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:16px;">
          BirkyStudio is not software you log into and work. It is an operator that runs in the background. The Base Agent ($1,297 solo, from $2,997 for a team) reads every website and WhatsApp enquiry, sorts it, saves it to a Notion CRM built for agents, answers it instantly, and follows up automatically, in English and Spanish. The CRM is included free, so you are not paying a subscription for a database, and there is no call meter or action counter watching how much it runs.
        </p>
        <p style="color:var(--bs-text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:16px;">
          The front desk is the part that overlaps with Allo, and here is exactly what you get. The Voice Receptionist is $550 one time plus Vapi usage of about $30 to $50 a month, and it answers calls 24/7 in English and Spanish, qualifies the caller, takes the message and books the showing into your calendar. The Text Receptionist is $297 one time and holds full AI conversations on WhatsApp, which is the channel Allo does not cover at all. Voice plus text together is $847 once, which is less than a year of Allo's $64 a month, and after that there is no monthly fee to answer anything, only the Vapi usage on the calls themselves. That is the honest arithmetic and it is the whole reason this page exists: we are not the cheapest way to answer a phone in year one, we are the cheapest way to answer both a phone and a WhatsApp for as long as you sell.
        </p>
        <p style="color:var(--bs-text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:16px;">
          Websites are the other half of what we sell, and they are deliberately the opposite of a platform: Starter $499 for 1 to 3 pages, Professional $999 for a 4 to 7 page bilingual site, Premium $1,999 for 10+ pages with a blog, all one-time, delivered in days, on your own account with the code in your hands. There is a $130 CMS add-on if you want to edit it yourself. What we do not have is the telephony layer Allo is good at: we are not a phone system, we do not supply the numbers or the IVR or the porting, and we do not run an SDR or a parallel dialer. If you need a business phone system, buy one, and Allo is a reasonable one. We sit in front of it as the answering layer that also covers the message apps.
        </p>
