            → <strong style="color:white;">BirkyStudio</strong>. Bilingual English and Spanish is standard in both the receptionist and the website, not an upgrade. Allo is English first: it advertises a French voice among its receptionist options but makes no Spanish claim, so an after-hours call in Spanish gets an English greeting unless a person picks up. In real estate, where a large share of buyers are Spanish speaking, that is the difference between a booked showing and a missed one.
