        </div>

        <div style="background:rgba(255,255,255,0.05);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);border-radius:16px;padding:24px;">
          <h3 style="color:white;font-size:1.1rem;margin-bottom:8px;">📱 You want a proper business phone system, not just an answering layer</h3>
          <p style="color:var(--bs-text);line-height:1.8;margin:0;">
            → <strong style="color:white;">Allo</strong>. We are not a phone system and we do not pretend to be one. Allo hands you the numbers, the porting, the IVR, the shared inbox, the SMS, the call recording and, on the add-on, a parallel dialer for the whole team, all in a mobile app that is genuinely the product rather than a cut-down copy. If you want one place for every line in the business, buy Allo. BirkyStudio sits in front of it as the answering layer that also covers the message apps.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div style="background:rgba(255,255,255,0.05);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);border-radius:16px;padding:24px;">
          <h3 style="color:white;font-size:1.1rem;margin-bottom:8px;">💸 You are tired of paying monthly for something you will never own</h3>
          <p style="color:var(--bs-text);line-height:1.8;margin:0;">
            → <strong style="color:white;">BirkyStudio</strong>. This is arithmetic rather than preference. Allo is about $64 a month for one agent and the receptionist, every month, and stopping the payment stops the number. Voice plus WhatsApp with us is $847 once, and with Vapi usage of about $40 a month that is roughly level with Allo over three years, after which the build is still yours and there is no phone bill to answer anything. If you plan to still be selling in three years, the one-time purchase is the cheaper one. If you are not sure you will still be running AI in six months, Allo is the better bet and easier to leave.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div style="background:rgba(255,255,255,0.05);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);border-radius:16px;padding:24px;">
          <h3 style="color:white;font-size:1.1rem;margin-bottom:8px;">👥 You are buying for a team, not just yourself</h3>
          <p style="color:var(--bs-text);line-height:1.8;margin:0;">
            → <strong style="color:white;">Allo</strong>, on the phone system, and neither of us on the rest. Allo is built for teams: unlimited seats, each with its own number, a shared inbox, the AI receptionist on the shared line, and per-seat billing that scales from one to two hundred and fifty people. For a five person team with the receptionist that is about $2,304 a year, which is fair. BirkyStudio's business tier starts at $2,997 one-time and is not multiplied by seat, but we do not sell lead routing, commissions or back office either. For a brokerage that wants one system for IDX, routing and recruiting, read the BoldTrail and Sierra Interactive pages on this site instead.
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>

      <!-- Final Recommendation -->
      <div style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--bs-bg-raised),var(--bs-bg-raised));border-radius:16px;padding:32px;margin-bottom:64px;border:1px solid rgba(255,45,149,0.3);">
        <h2 style="color:white;font-size:1.3rem;margin-bottom:16px;">🏆 The Bottom Line</h2>
        <p style="color:var(--bs-text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:16px;">
          If all you need is your phone answered, <strong style="color:white;">buy Allo, use the 3 day free trial, and do not look back</strong>. It is the cheapest unlimited AI call answering in the category, the price is published before you speak to anyone, the minutes are flat with no per minute meter, the number is yours to port, SMS and recording are included, the app is mobile first, and there is no setup fee and no contract. It is honest that the AI answers rather than dials. Our pricing pages on competitors such as Smith.ai, Goodcall, RingCentral and CloudTalk charge more for less on the lines that matter, and this page says so on purpose. For a solo agent whose only leak is the phone, Allo is the right buy and we would be lying to claim otherwise.
        </p>
        <p style="color:var(--bs-text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:16px;">
          But be equally clear about the four things a phone system cannot do. Allo holds no WhatsApp conversation, so the buyer who messages on Sunday still waits. It is English first, with no Spanish claim for the AI receptionist. It meters the meters you forgot about, because every agent needs a seat and the receptionist adds one more, so a five person team with the receptionist is about $2,304 a year, every year, and stopping the payment stops the number. And it is narrower than the word AI suggests: no website, no leads, no campaign. <strong style="color:white;">BirkyStudio is a different shape of purchase.</strong> The Voice Receptionist answers calls 24/7 in English and Spanish for $550 once plus Vapi usage, the WhatsApp Text Receptionist is $297 once and covers the channel Allo cannot reach, The Base Agent is $1,297 once with the Notion CRM included free, and the website and its pages stay yours whether or not we ever speak again.
        </p>
        <p style="color:var(--bs-text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:24px;">
          The cleanest way to see it: Allo is what you buy when your problem is the phone line. BirkyStudio is what you buy when your problem is every way a lead can arrive, in two languages, and you would rather own the operator than rent it. If both are true, run both, because a phone system and an answering operator do not overlap and plenty of agents who last run exactly that.<br><br>
          <strong style="color:white;">Choose Allo if:</strong> you want the cheapest unlimited call answering, a complete phone system with numbers and SMS, and a flat published price you can leave any month.<br><br>
          <strong style="color:white;">Choose BirkyStudio if:</strong> you want your phone and WhatsApp answered 24/7 in English and Spanish, follow-up that sends itself, verified prospects you own, and a one-time price instead of a seat you rent forever.
        </p>
