      </div>

      <!-- FAQ -->
      <h2 id="faq" style="font-size:1.6rem;font-weight:700;color:white;margin-bottom:16px;">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <div style="margin-bottom:48px;">

        <details style="padding:20px;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.03);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);border-radius:12px;margin-bottom:12px;">
          <summary style="color:white;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer;list-style:none;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;">
            <span>How much does Allo cost?</span>
            <span style="font-size:0.9rem;">▼</span>
          </summary>
          <div style="margin-top:12px;color:var(--bs-text);line-height:1.8;">
            Allo publishes its prices, which already puts it ahead of most vendors in this category. A Business seat is $32 a month billed yearly, or $45 month to month, and the AI Receptionist is an add-on that costs one more seat per agent, $32 a month billed yearly or $45 month to month. So one agent with the receptionist pays the equivalent of about $64 a month billed yearly, or about $90 a month on monthly billing, which is $768 and $1,080 for the year. There is no per minute meter, so a busy week costs the same as a quiet one. An extra phone number starts at $5 a month, the Power Dialer is a flat $50 a month for the whole team, and a HIPAA Business Associate Agreement is $50 a month for the whole workspace. There are no setup fees and no contracts, seat changes are prorated, and every plan starts with a 3 day free trial with the AI add-on enabled.
          </div>
        </details>

        <details style="padding:20px;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.03);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);border-radius:12px;margin-bottom:12px;">
          <summary style="color:white;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer;list-style:none;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;">
            <span>Does Allo answer WhatsApp messages?</span>
            <span style="font-size:0.9rem;">▼</span>
          </summary>
          <div style="margin-top:12px;color:var(--bs-text);line-height:1.8;">
            No. Allo is a phone system and its AI receptionist answers inbound calls, sends an SMS text back to a missed call and updates your CRM after every call, but it does not hold an AI conversation on WhatsApp. For a lot of real estate buyers, especially in Latin America, the United States and Europe, WhatsApp is where the first message actually arrives, and a chat that waits until someone picks it up is a lead that waits. BirkyStudio's Text Receptionist is $297 one time and holds full WhatsApp conversations 24/7 in English and Spanish, so it answers the channel Allo does not cover.
          </div>
        </details>

        <details style="padding:20px;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.03);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);border-radius:12px;margin-bottom:12px;">
          <summary style="color:white;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer;list-style:none;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;">
            <span>Does Allo's AI make outbound calls?</span>
            <span style="font-size:0.9rem;">▼</span>
          </summary>
          <div style="margin-top:12px;color:var(--bs-text);line-height:1.8;">
            No, and Allo is unusually honest about it. Its own comparison page states that today the AI receptionist answers calls and does not place them, so outbound calling stays with the people on your team, helped by the $50 a month Power Dialer and the Ultra plan's AI SDR. BirkyStudio is not a dialer either, and we are not going to pretend otherwise. What we do place is the follow-up: The Base Agent reads every website and WhatsApp enquiry, saves it and answers it instantly, then follows up automatically without you approving each send, in English and Spanish. The $1,997 Lead Generation Pack pairs that with a verified prospect list and outreach, which is about who to contact rather than how fast the phone dials.
          </div>
        </details>

        <details style="padding:20px;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.03);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);border-radius:12px;margin-bottom:12px;">
          <summary style="color:white;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer;list-style:none;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;">
            <span>How is Allo different from BirkyStudio's AI Receptionist?</span>
            <span style="font-size:0.9rem;">▼</span>
          </summary>
          <div style="margin-top:12px;color:var(--bs-text);line-height:1.8;">
            They both answer the phone around the clock, which is why this page pairs them. The difference is the shape of the purchase and the width of the answer. Allo is a phone system you operate, sold per seat, on subscription every month, where the AI receptionist is an add-on and stopping the payment stops the number. BirkyStudio builds it for you once: the Voice Receptionist is $550 one time plus Vapi usage of about $30 to $50 a month, and it answers calls 24/7 in English and Spanish, not English first. Add the $297 WhatsApp Text Receptionist and the $1,297 Base Agent and one operator covers phone, WhatsApp and website enquiries into a Notion CRM included free. Allo wins on being a complete phone system with porting, SMS and an IVR at the lowest unlimited price in the category. We win on covering the inbox as well as the phone line, in two languages, for a one time price.
          </div>
        </details>

        <details style="padding:20px;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.03);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);border-radius:12px;margin-bottom:12px;">
          <summary style="color:white;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer;list-style:none;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;">
            <span>Does Allo have a contract, a setup fee or a free trial?</span>
            <span style="font-size:0.9rem;">▼</span>
          </summary>
          <div style="margin-top:12px;color:var(--bs-text);line-height:1.8;">
            This is a place where Allo is genuinely clean and worth saying plainly. There are no setup fees and no contracts, you can upgrade, downgrade or cancel whenever you want, changes to seats are prorated so you never pay for seats you do not use, and every plan starts with a 3 day free trial with the AI add-on enabled for the length of the trial, though a card is required. That is a fairer buying experience than Sierra Interactive's twelve month agreement or CINC's quoted pricing. BirkyStudio is also contract free, with no minimum term and a 30 day money back guarantee on the build.
          </div>
        </details>

        <details style="padding:20px;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.03);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);border-radius:12px;margin-bottom:12px;">
          <summary style="color:white;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer;list-style:none;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;">
            <span>Does Allo include a website or lead generation?</span>
            <span style="font-size:0.9rem;">▼</span>
          </summary>
          <div style="margin-top:12px;color:var(--bs-text);line-height:1.8;">
            No to both. Allo is a business phone system, so it supplies none of its own leads and it does not build a website. What it does is answer and log the calls you already get, sync them to the CRM you already pay for through HubSpot, Pipedrive, Attio, Salesforce or Zapier, and text back the ones you miss. If you want leads to call, BirkyStudio's Verified Prospect List at $497 or $997 one time is a file of verified, enriched, scored prospects you own, not a rented stream, and our websites at $499, $999 and $1,999 one time are yours with the code in your hands. If you need an IDX listing site, that comes from a platform such as BoldTrail, Sierra Interactive or Placester.
          </div>
        </details>

        <details style="padding:20px;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.03);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);border-radius:12px;margin-bottom:12px;">
          <summary style="color:white;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer;list-style:none;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;">
            <span>What do Allo's own reviewers say?</span>
            <span style="font-size:0.9rem;">▼</span>
          </summary>
          <div style="margin-top:12px;color:var(--bs-text);line-height:1.8;">
            Mostly good, with two honest gaps. G2 shows roughly 4.6 to 4.7 out of 5 across about 200 reviews, and the things reviewers praise are the flat unlimited price, the mobile first design, the CRM sync and the AI receptionist itself. G2's own summary of the downsides lists a lack of picture messaging, SMS features reviewers miss, some call quality and app lag, and a desktop app that several users call weaker than the mobile app. One reviewer wrote that it was a shame SMS messages are no longer unlimited, and another described terrible call quality with no update for over a month. Trustpilot is thinner: 4.2 out of 5 across 24 reviews, positive on call clarity and support, with a few 1 star reviews about being charged after cancelling. None of that changes the value case, but it is the same lesson as always: use the free trial rather than trusting a page like this one, including ours.
          </div>
        </details>

      </div>

